\vspace*{12\baselineskip}
\section{Calibration and External Cases}
\subsection{Synthetic Benchmark}
The claim-module policy is also evaluated where the mechanism and claim label are
known before evaluation. A repeated synthetic temporal benchmark covers 14 regimes
over 30 seeds each, including correlated features, omitted confounding, temporal
and geographic shift, and leakage. GT permit labels define six permissible
regimes and are used only for scoring; policy permit is computed from observable
Module A, B, and E outputs. Ungated explanations falsely permit 240 of 240
invalid runs (100.0\%, 95\% CI [98.4,100.0]); the observable A+B+E policy falsely permits
\SyntheticPolicyFalsePermissions{} invalid runs (\SyntheticPolicyFalsePermissionRate{},
95\% CI [65.2,76.6]) while falsely abstaining on
\SyntheticPolicyFalseAbstentions{} valid runs
(\SyntheticPolicyFalseAbstentionRate{}, 95\% CI [7.3,16.5]). Its permission rate
is \SyntheticPolicyPermissionRate{}, sensitivity \SyntheticPolicySensitivity{},
and specificity \SyntheticPolicySpecificity{}.

The observable modules cannot reliably identify all structurally invalid regimes:
omitted confounding, geographic shift, leakage, and correlated features are
permitted in 30/30 seeds, and temporal drift in 29/30. These are false
permissions, not successful abstentions.

